{"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/Readium\/documentation\/Readium"]]},"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"The Timeline API lays out the table of contents of a publication on its reading order. It answers questions such as “which chapter am I in?”, “what is the next chapter?” or “how much is left in this chapter?”. Use it to show where each chapter starts in a table of contents, to display the current chapter in a running header, to step through the chapters of a publication, or to pause the playback at the end of an audiobook chapter."}],"kind":"article","schemaVersion":{"major":0,"minor":3,"patch":0},"primaryContentSections":[{"content":[{"anchor":"overview","type":"heading","text":"Overview","level":2},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"In this guide, a "},{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"chapter"}]},{"type":"text","text":" is any entry of the table of contents, at any depth, such as Part I, Chapter 2 or Section 2.2 in the examples below."}]},{"name":"Important","type":"aside","style":"important","content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The Timeline API is experimental and may change in a future release. To use it, import "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"ReadiumShared"},{"type":"text","text":" with the "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"ExperimentalTimeline"},{"type":"text","text":" SPI:"}]},{"type":"codeListing","syntax":"swift","code":["@_spi(ExperimentalTimeline) import ReadiumShared"]}]},{"anchor":"Understanding-the-timeline","type":"heading","text":"Understanding the timeline","level":2},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The examples of this guide use two publications."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"An "},{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"audiobook"}]},{"type":"text","text":" made of four tracks: "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"intro.mp3"},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"track1.mp3"},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"track2.mp3"},{"type":"text","text":" and "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"track3.mp3"},{"type":"text","text":". Its table of contents is:"}]},{"type":"unorderedList","items":[{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Part I → "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"track1.mp3#t=287"}]},{"type":"unorderedList","items":[{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Chapter 1 → ","type":"text"},{"code":"track1.mp3#t=541","type":"codeVoice"}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Chapter 2 → ","type":"text"},{"code":"track2.mp3","type":"codeVoice"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"items":[{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Scene 2.1 → "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"track2.mp3#t=642"}]}]}],"type":"unorderedList"}]}]}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Part II → "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"track3.mp3"}]},{"type":"unorderedList","items":[{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Chapter 3 → ","type":"text"},{"code":"track3.mp3#t=263","type":"codeVoice"}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Bonus → ","type":"text"},{"code":"bonus.mp3","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", which is not in the reading order","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}]}]}]}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"A "},{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"reflowable EPUB"}]},{"type":"text","text":" made of five resources: "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"preface.xhtml"},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"chapter1.xhtml"},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"chapter2.xhtml"},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"chapter2-part2.xhtml"},{"type":"text","text":" and "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"chapter3.xhtml"},{"type":"text","text":". Its table of contents is:"}]},{"type":"unorderedList","items":[{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Chapter 1 → "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"chapter1.xhtml"}]}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Chapter 2 → "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"chapter2.xhtml"}]},{"type":"unorderedList","items":[{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Section 2.1 → ","type":"text"},{"code":"chapter2.xhtml#section1","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", which is not placed (see ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"#entries-of-an-epub"},{"text":")","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Section 2.2 → ","type":"text"},{"code":"chapter2-part2.xhtml","type":"codeVoice"}],"type":"paragraph"}]}]}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Chapter 3 → "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"chapter3.xhtml"}]}]}]},{"anchor":"Positions-on-the-timeline","type":"heading","text":"Positions on the timeline","level":3},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The reading order forms one continuous line, from the start of the publication to its end. Each resource takes the length it has in the natural unit of the publication: its duration in an audiobook, its number of pages in a PDF, or its number of positions in a reflowable EPUB."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"In the audiobook, the line lasts 55 minutes and 8 seconds."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"image","identifier":"timeline-positions.svg"}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"In the EPUB, the line is made of the 40 positions of the publication. A position is a stable chunk of content, independent of the screen size and font size."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"image","identifier":"timeline-epub-positions.svg"}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"A "},{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"TimelinePosition"}]},{"type":"text","text":" is a point on this line. It is located by its reading order index and its offset in the resource. Its other properties are derived from these two. The positions above, 5 minutes into "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"track2.mp3"},{"type":"text","text":" and halfway through "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"chapter2.xhtml"},{"type":"text","text":", are:"}]},{"rows":[[[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Property"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Description"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Audiobook"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"EPUB"}]}]],[[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"readingOrderIndex"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Index of the resource in the reading order."}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"2"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"2"}]}]],[[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"offset"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Offset in the resource, in a unit chosen by the timeline. Only compare it within a resource."}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"300"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"0.5"}]}]],[[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"coordinate"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Where the position stands in the publication, in its natural unit."}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":".time(1519)"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":".position(20)"}]}]],[[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"progression"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Progression in the resource, from 0 to 1."}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"0.24"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"0.5"}]}]],[[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"totalProgression"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Progression in the publication, from 0 to 1."}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"0.46"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"0.475"}]}]]],"type":"table","header":"row"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Call "},{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"code":"timeline.position(of:)","type":"codeVoice"}]},{"type":"text","text":" to get the position of a "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Locator"},{"type":"text","text":", such as the current location of the Navigator. It returns "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"nil"},{"type":"text","text":" when the locator is outside the reading order."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"code":"TimelinePosition","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" is not "},{"code":"Comparable","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":", because two positions at the same place can differ in their derived properties. Use "},{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"code":"isBefore(_:)","type":"codeVoice"}]},{"text":" to order them.","type":"text"}]},{"type":"heading","level":4,"anchor":"Units","text":"Units"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"A ","type":"text"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"TimelineCoordinate"}],"type":"strong"},{"text":" tells where a position stands, and a ","type":"text"},{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"code":"TimelineLength","type":"codeVoice"}]},{"text":" measures the distance between two positions, in the natural unit of the publication:","type":"text"}]},{"rows":[[[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Publication","type":"text"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Coordinate","type":"text"}]}],[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Length","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}]],[[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Audiobook","type":"text"}]}],[{"inlineContent":[{"code":".time(seconds)","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" since the start","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"code":".duration(seconds)","type":"codeVoice"}]}]],[[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"PDF","type":"text"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":".page(number)"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"code":".pages(count)","type":"codeVoice"}]}]],[[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Comic (CBZ, DiViNa)"}],"type":"paragraph"}],[{"inlineContent":[{"code":".page(number)","type":"codeVoice"}],"type":"paragraph"}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":".pages(count)"}]}]],[[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Fixed-layout EPUB","type":"text"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"code":".page(number)","type":"codeVoice"}]}],[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":".pages(count)"}],"type":"paragraph"}]],[[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Reflowable EPUB, HTML publication"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"code":".position(number)","type":"codeVoice"}]}],[{"inlineContent":[{"code":".positions(count)","type":"codeVoice"}],"type":"paragraph"}]]],"type":"table","header":"row"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"An EPUB is measured in pages only when all its resources have a fixed layout. An EPUB mixing reflowable and fixed-layout resources is measured in positions."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Page and position numbers start at 1. A "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":".position"},{"type":"text","text":" matches the "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"locations.position"},{"type":"text","text":" of a "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Locator"},{"type":"text","text":", see the "},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/Readium\/documentation\/Readium\/Navigator#Displaying-the-number-of-positions","overridingTitle":"Navigator guide","overridingTitleInlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Navigator guide"}]},{"type":"text","text":" for more about positions."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Call "},{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"timeline.length(from:to:)"}]},{"type":"text","text":" to measure the distance between two positions."}]},{"type":"aside","name":"Note","style":"note","content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The end of a chapter, or of the publication, is exclusive: it is one past its last page or position."}]}]},{"anchor":"Table-of-contents-entries","type":"heading","level":3,"text":"Table of contents entries"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"code":"timeline.toc","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" is a "},{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"TimelineTOC"}]},{"type":"text","text":", a tree of "},{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"TimelineTOCEntry"}]},{"type":"text","text":" mirroring the table of contents of the publication. Each entry has a "},{"code":"title","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":", a "},{"code":"link","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" and its "},{"code":"children","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":". The "},{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"depth"}]},{"type":"text","text":" of an entry is its level in the tree, starting at 1 for the top level."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"To place the entries on the timeline, the tree is flattened in pre-order: each entry comes before its children, and the children come before the next sibling of their parent."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"image","identifier":"timeline-toc-tree.svg"}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Each entry then gets a range on the timeline:"}]},{"items":[{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"It starts where its link points, in its "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"start"},{"type":"text","text":" property. "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"track1.mp3#t=287"},{"type":"text","text":" is 4:47 into "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"track1.mp3"},{"type":"text","text":", which starts at 4:52, so Part I starts at 9:39."}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"It ends at the start of the next placed entry after its subtree, or at the end of the publication, in its "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"end"},{"type":"text","text":" property. Part I ends where Part II starts, at 41:27."}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Its "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"length"},{"type":"text","text":" is the distance from its start to its end."}],"type":"paragraph"}]}],"type":"unorderedList"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"A parent therefore contains its children, and owns the gap before its first child: Part I alone covers 9:39 to 13:53."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"image","identifier":"timeline-toc-ranges.svg"}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"An entry cannot be placed when its link points outside the reading order, like Bonus, or before the start of the previous placed entry in pre-order. It keeps its place in the tree, but its "},{"code":"start","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"code":"end","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" and "},{"code":"length","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" are "},{"code":"nil","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":"."}]},{"anchor":"Segments","type":"heading","level":3,"text":"Segments"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The entries overlap: at 25:19, you are both in Part I and in Chapter 2. "},{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"timeline.segments(maxDepth:)"}]},{"type":"text","text":" cuts the reading order into "},{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"TimelineSegment"}]},{"type":"text","text":" values following each other from the start of the publication to its end, without gaps or overlaps. Each segment matches the deepest entry containing it, in its "},{"code":"tocEntry","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" property."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"image","identifier":"timeline-segments.svg"}]},{"items":[{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"A segment ends where another entry takes over. The segment of Part I ends at 13:53, where Chapter 1 starts, while the entry Part I goes on until 41:27."}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Outside any entry, such as before the first one or in a publication without a table of contents, there is one segment without entry per resource. Its "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"tocEntry"},{"type":"text","text":" is "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"nil"},{"type":"text","text":". The segments therefore always cover the whole publication."}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"code":"maxDepth","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" ignores the deeper entries: their positions belong to the segment of their closest ancestor within this depth. With ","type":"text"},{"code":"maxDepth: 1","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", there is one segment per part.","type":"text"}]}]}],"type":"unorderedList"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"In the EPUB, the preface is a segment without entry, and Section 2.2 splits Chapter 2 in two segments, unless you ignore it with ","type":"text"},{"code":"maxDepth: 1","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":". Section 2.1 is not placed, as explained in "},{"isActive":true,"overridingTitle":"Limitations","type":"reference","overridingTitleInlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Limitations"}],"identifier":"#entries-of-an-epub"},{"type":"text","text":"."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"image","identifier":"timeline-epub-segments.svg"}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"The ","type":"text"},{"code":"link","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" of a segment points to its start, so that you can go there with the Navigator.","type":"text"}]},{"anchor":"Getting-the-timeline-of-a-publication","type":"heading","level":2,"text":"Getting the timeline of a publication"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Call ","type":"text"},{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"publication.timeline()"}]},{"type":"text","text":" to build the timeline, or get "},{"code":"nil","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" when the publication has no timeline service."}]},{"type":"codeListing","syntax":"swift","code":["@_spi(ExperimentalTimeline) import ReadiumShared","","let timeline: Timeline?","do {","    timeline = try await publication.timeline()","} catch {","    print(\"Failed to build the timeline: \\(error)\")","    timeline = nil","}","","guard let timeline else {","    \/\/ Hide the features depending on the timeline.","    return","}","","let segments = timeline.segments()"]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"code":"segments(maxDepth:)","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" builds a new "},{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"TimelineSegments"}]},{"type":"text","text":" collection at each call. You are responsible for keeping it while the publication is open, to locate each new location."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"When the table of contents of the publication fails to load, you get a timeline without entries, whose segments still cover each resource."}]},{"anchor":"Displaying-the-table-of-contents","type":"heading","level":2,"text":"Displaying the table of contents"},{"type":"heading","level":3,"anchor":"Showing-where-each-entry-stands","text":"Showing where each entry stands"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Show the time, page or position where each entry starts.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"type":"codeListing","syntax":"swift","code":["extension TimelineTOCEntry {","    var trailingLabel: String? {","        switch start?.coordinate {","        case let .page(number), let .position(number):","            return \"\\(number)\"","        case let .time(seconds):","            return Duration.seconds(seconds).formatted(.time(pattern: .hourMinuteSecond))","        case nil:","            return nil","        }","    }","","    \/\/\/ Children of the entry, or `nil` for a leaf, as expected by `List`.","    var nestedEntries: [TimelineTOCEntry]? {","        children.isEmpty ? nil : children","    }","}","","struct TableOfContentsView: View {","    let toc: TimelineTOC","    let onSelect: (ReadiumShared.Link) -> Void","","    var body: some View {","        List(toc.entries, children: \\.nestedEntries) { entry in","            Button {","                onSelect(entry.link)","            } label: {","                HStack {","                    Text(entry.title)","                    Spacer()","                    if let label = entry.trailingLabel {","                        Text(label)","                            .monospacedDigit()","                            .foregroundStyle(.secondary)","                    }","                }","            }","        }","    }","}"]},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"When the user selects an entry, go to its link with "},{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"code":"navigator.go(to:)","type":"codeVoice"}]},{"text":".","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"type":"codeListing","syntax":"swift","code":["await navigator.go(to: link)"]},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"An entry that cannot be placed has no start nor length, so it shows its title only. Keep it in the list: its link may still be valid for the Navigator, such as an EPUB entry pointing to an anchor or outside the reading order (see "},{"type":"reference","overridingTitle":"Limitations","identifier":"#entries-of-an-epub","overridingTitleInlineContent":[{"text":"Limitations","type":"text"}],"isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":")."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"anchor":"Marking-the-current-entry","type":"heading","level":3,"text":"Marking the current entry"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The "},{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"code":"segment(containing:)","type":"codeVoice"}]},{"type":"text","text":" method of "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"TimelineSegments"},{"type":"text","text":" returns the segment containing a "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Locator"},{"type":"text","text":", whose "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"tocEntry"},{"type":"text","text":" is the current entry of the table of contents. Before the first entry, the segment has no "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"tocEntry"},{"type":"text","text":". The method returns "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"nil"},{"type":"text","text":" only when the "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Locator"},{"type":"text","text":" is outside the reading order."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"type":"codeListing","syntax":"swift","code":["let currentEntry = navigator.currentLocation","    .flatMap { segments.segment(containing: $0) }?","    .tocEntry"]},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"toc.path(to:)"}]},{"type":"text","text":" returns the entries from the top level down to an entry, such as "},{"code":"[Part I, Chapter 2]","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" at 25:19. Use it to:"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"type":"unorderedList","items":[{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"expand the ancestors of the current entry when the table of contents opens, then scroll to it;"}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"mark the current entry, or its closest ancestor when the entry is hidden in a collapsed row."}],"type":"paragraph"}]}]},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"In this sketch, "},{"code":"expandedIDs","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" holds the IDs of the expanded rows of your list, and "},{"code":"scrollTo","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" scrolls the list with a "},{"code":"ScrollViewReader","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":"."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"type":"codeListing","syntax":"swift","code":["let currentPath = currentEntry.map { toc.path(to: $0).map(\\.id) } ?? []","","\/\/ When the table of contents opens.","expandedIDs.formUnion(currentPath.dropLast())","scrollTo(currentPath.last)","","\/\/ For each visible row.","let isCurrent = entry.id == currentPath.last","    || (currentPath.contains(entry.id) && !expandedIDs.contains(entry.id))","","Text(entry.title)","    .fontWeight(isCurrent ? .semibold : .regular)","    .accessibilityAddTraits(isCurrent ? .isSelected : [])"]},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"In the preface of the EPUB, there is no current entry, so no row is marked. An entry keeps its "},{"code":"id","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" when the timeline is rebuilt from the same table of contents, so you can keep the expanded entries across openings of the table of contents."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"anchor":"Locating-the-current-chapter","type":"heading","level":2,"text":"Locating the current chapter"},{"inlineContent":[{"code":"segment(containing:)","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" runs a binary search, so you can call it at each location change of the Navigator. Pick the maximum depth of a “chapter” with the ","type":"text"},{"code":"maxDepth","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" parameter of ","type":"text"},{"code":"segments(maxDepth:)","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":".","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"style":"tip","content":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"To detect when the reader enters another chapter, compare the "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"start"},{"type":"text","text":" of the segments rather than the segments themselves. The equality of two segments compares their entries with their whole subtree, while the start of a segment is unique within its collection."}],"type":"paragraph"}],"type":"aside","name":"Tip"},{"anchor":"Breadcrumbs-as-running-header","type":"heading","level":3,"text":"Breadcrumbs as running header"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Display the current entry with its ancestors.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"type":"codeListing","syntax":"swift","code":["func header(at locator: Locator) -> String? {","    guard","        let segment = segments.segment(containing: locator),","        let entry = segment.tocEntry","    else {","        return nil","    }","    return timeline.toc.path(to: entry)","        .map(\\.title)","        .joined(separator: \" › \")","}"]},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"At 25:19, the header is “Part I › Chapter 2”.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"anchor":"Previous-and-next-chapter","type":"heading","level":3,"text":"Previous and next chapter"},{"inlineContent":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"segment(before:)"}],"type":"strong"},{"text":" and ","type":"text"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"segment(after:)"}],"type":"strong"},{"text":" return the adjacent segments, which you can go to with their ","type":"text"},{"code":"link","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":". As the segments cover the whole publication, the listener can also reach the tracks before the first chapter.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"type":"codeListing","syntax":"swift","code":["func goToNextChapter() async {","    guard","        let locator = navigator.currentLocation,","        let current = segments.segment(containing: locator),","        let next = segments.segment(after: current)","    else {","        return","    }","    await navigator.go(to: next.link)","}"]},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Like most audio players, the “previous” button can restart the current chapter, and go to the previous one only near its start:","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"type":"codeListing","syntax":"swift","code":["func goToPreviousChapter() async {","    guard","        let locator = navigator.currentLocation,","        let position = timeline.position(of: locator),","        let current = segments.segment(containing: locator)","    else {","        return","    }","","    let elapsed = timeline.length(from: current.start, to: position)?.seconds ?? 0","    let target = elapsed > 3 ? current : segments.segment(before: current) ?? current","    await navigator.go(to: target.link)","}"]},{"anchor":"Measuring-what-is-left-in-the-chapter","type":"heading","level":3,"text":"Measuring what is left in the chapter"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Measure the length from the current position to the end of its segment. The ","type":"text"},{"code":"end","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" of the last segment is ","type":"text"},{"code":"nil","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" when the length of the last resource is unknown.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"type":"codeListing","syntax":"swift","code":["func remainingInChapter(at locator: Locator) -> TimelineLength? {","    guard","        let position = timeline.position(of: locator),","        let end = segments.segment(containing: locator)?.end","    else {","        return nil","    }","    return timeline.length(from: position, to: end)","}"]},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"At position 20 of the EPUB, the length is ","type":"text"},{"code":".positions(6)","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":": positions 20 to 25 are left before Section 2.2. At 25:19 in the audiobook, it is ","type":"text"},{"code":".duration(342)","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":": 5:42 are left before Scene 2.1.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"anchor":"Marking-the-chapters-on-the-progress-bar-of-a-resource","type":"heading","level":3,"text":"Marking the chapters on the progress bar of a resource"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"When your progress bar shows the progression in the current resource, such as the current track of an audiobook, mark where each chapter starts on it. "},{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"segments(in:)"}]},{"type":"text","text":" returns the segments of a single resource, clipped to it. The "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"progression"},{"type":"text","text":" of their start goes from 0 to 1 in the resource."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"type":"codeListing","syntax":"swift","code":["let marks = segments.segments(in: locator.href)","    .compactMap(\\.start.progression)","    .filter { $0 > 0 }"]},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"In "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"track1.mp3"},{"type":"text","text":", the marks are at 0.31 for Part I and 0.58 for Chapter 1."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"anchor":"Limitations","type":"heading","level":2,"text":"Limitations"},{"anchor":"Entries-of-an-EPUB","type":"heading","level":3,"text":"Entries of an EPUB"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The timeline of an EPUB currently places only the first entry pointing to each resource, at the start of the resource. Section 2.1 points to an anchor in "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"chapter2.xhtml"},{"type":"text","text":", whose first entry is Chapter 2, so it is not placed. Section 2.2 is the first entry pointing to "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"chapter2-part2.xhtml"},{"type":"text","text":", so it starts there. Chapter 2 covers both of its resources, up to Chapter 3."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"image","identifier":"timeline-epub-toc-ranges.svg"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The current entry of an EPUB is therefore precise to the resource."}]},{"type":"heading","level":3,"anchor":"Unknown-lengths","text":"Unknown lengths"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"When the length of a resource is unknown, such as an audiobook without the ","type":"text"},{"code":"duration","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" of its tracks, or a publication whose positions cannot be computed, the coordinates, progressions and lengths depending on it are ","type":"text"},{"code":"nil","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":". The entries are still placed, and the segments still locate the current chapter.","type":"text"}]}],"kind":"content"}],"identifier":{"interfaceLanguage":"swift","url":"doc:\/\/Readium\/documentation\/Readium\/Timeline"},"variants":[{"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}],"paths":["\/documentation\/readium\/timeline"]}],"metadata":{"roleHeading":"Article","title":"Timeline","role":"article"},"sections":[],"seeAlsoSections":[{"title":"Guides","generated":true,"anchor":"Guides","identifiers":["doc:\/\/Readium\/documentation\/Readium\/Getting-Started","doc:\/\/Readium\/documentation\/Readium\/Migration-Guide","doc:\/\/Readium\/documentation\/Readium\/Open-Publication","doc:\/\/Readium\/documentation\/Readium\/NavigatorOverview","doc:\/\/Readium\/documentation\/Readium\/Content","doc:\/\/Readium\/documentation\/Readium\/Search","doc:\/\/Readium\/documentation\/Readium\/TTS","doc:\/\/Readium\/documentation\/Readium\/Accessibility","doc:\/\/Readium\/documentation\/Readium\/Readium-LCP"]}],"references":{"doc://Readium/documentation/Readium/TTS":{"type":"topic","identifier":"doc:\/\/Readium\/documentation\/Readium\/TTS","title":"Text-to-speech","abstract":[],"url":"\/documentation\/readium\/tts","kind":"article","role":"article"},"doc://Readium/documentation/Readium/Migration-Guide":{"kind":"article","title":"Migration Guide","identifier":"doc:\/\/Readium\/documentation\/Readium\/Migration-Guide","role":"article","url":"\/documentation\/readium\/migration-guide","type":"topic","abstract":[{"text":"All migration steps necessary in reading apps to upgrade to major versions of the Swift Readium toolkit will be documented in this file.","type":"text"}]},"doc://Readium/documentation/Readium/Getting-Started":{"title":"Getting started","url":"\/documentation\/readium\/getting-started","role":"article","identif